 "toleranceNote": "Chrome (mock reference) lays text out with integer-rounded glyph advances, Skia with fractional ones: 12-14px text is 2-4% wider in the reference. Only boxes whose width is the text (wrap-content: the meta lines, the FAB, the sort button) depend on that, and what is aligned to their right edge moves with them; every other box is fill/fixed and held to 1px. Search: the chips, the \"Temizle\" button and the \"önizleme\" chip are wrap-content too; the chips after the first move by the sum of the earlier ones' differences, and a title that ends where such a chip starts changes width with it. Stats: a tile's label is an inline <span> in a 21px line box (the body's 14px strut); Chrome's box is the 12px font's 15px content area, the app's the 20px line set in the 21px box.",
